meta {
  name: Create Order No Token
  type: http
  seq: 1
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/order
  body: json
  auth: none
}

body:json {
  {
    "items": [
      {
        "productId": "{{productId}}",
        "quantity": 1
      }
    ]
  }
}

docs {
  No Authorization header at all — unlike product/inventory-service, order-service
  validates the JWT itself (OrderSecurityFilter + anyRequest().authenticated()), so this
  is rejected the same way on every environment:
  - "Gateway" (:8080): 401 UNAUTHORIZED, {"error": "Token não fornecido"} —
    rejected by api-gateway's JwtAuthenticationFilter before reaching order-service.
  - "OrderDirect" (:8081): 401 (Spring Security's default entry point — plain
    WWW-Authenticate challenge, no JSON body, since order-service has no custom
    AuthenticationEntryPoint like auth-service does) — order-service's own
    SecurityConfig rejects it independently, the defense-in-depth check working as
    intended (contrast with the No Token requests under product/inventory-service).
}
